1
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:11,678
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:12,341 --> 00:00:17,143
Huh, it's probably the military that put
these tripmines here in the first place.

3
00:00:17,143 --> 00:00:18,856
And they just go and run into them.

4
00:00:18,856 --> 00:00:23,451
I don't get it; they bomb each other,
they can't figure out who the civilians are,

5
00:00:23,451 --> 00:00:24,277
and they can't duck.

6
00:00:24,277 --> 00:00:25,834
Yeah, look, look how easy it is.

7
00:00:26,306 --> 00:00:27,644
Power slide!

8
00:00:27,644 --> 00:00:29,004
Yeah...

9
00:00:29,004 --> 00:00:30,801
I could be a rock star.

10
00:00:31,574 --> 00:00:34,334
Though, I... guess I'd have to
learn how to play guitar...

11
00:00:35,498 --> 00:00:39,890
And why does it wait so long for you to get
on here, but up there it's like a sprint?

12
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:42,067
Am I really the first
person to notice this?

13
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:43,377
[radio bleeping]
Oh, not this again!

14
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:44,525
[radio bleeping]

15
00:00:44,525 --> 00:00:45,734
[radio bleeping]
Please stop that!

16
00:00:45,734 --> 00:00:47,167
[radio bleeping]

17
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:50,078
[radio bleeping]
Okay, I asked nicely, what more can I do?

18
00:00:50,078 --> 00:00:51,931
[radio bleeping]
Who's punching in Morse code?

19
00:00:51,931 --> 00:00:53,968
[radio bleeping]
I don't speak Morse code!

20
00:00:55,049 --> 00:00:57,805
SO STOP THAT! IT'S RUDE!

21
00:00:57,805 --> 00:01:00,637
They're probably talking smack
about me on the radio.

22
00:01:00,637 --> 00:01:02,217
Well I'm not gonna stand for it!

23
00:01:02,217 --> 00:01:04,452
I've worked too hard to
get to where I am!

24
00:01:04,452 --> 00:01:06,367
I graduated from MIT!

25
00:01:07,201 --> 00:01:09,367
MY DIPLOMA'S WORTH MORE THAN YOUR LIFE!

26
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:14,105
Screw this, I'm just going to wait for
them to come around the corner again.

27
00:01:14,815 --> 00:01:15,650
OH SHIT!

28
00:01:16,001 --> 00:01:16,768
[explosion]

29
00:01:16,768 --> 00:01:18,925
Okay, natural selection.

30
00:01:18,925 --> 00:01:22,100
The dumb ones are all dead so
the survivors are a little bit smarter.

31
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,834
Ah hah hah! You asshole.

32
00:01:25,058 --> 00:01:25,767
DANCE!

33
00:01:26,574 --> 00:01:27,192
Oh, hold on.

34
00:01:27,192 --> 00:01:27,689
[explosion]

35
00:01:27,689 --> 00:01:28,500
Let me reload.

36
00:01:30,168 --> 00:01:30,734
Thanks.

37
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:33,166
Well, that was a learning experience.

38
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:34,701
And no one got hurt.

39
00:01:35,495 --> 00:01:36,434
Ohh...

40
00:01:37,373 --> 00:01:39,490
You guys had to ruin the moment.

41
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:43,537
Well, you guys are all bastards anyway,
so I guess nothing has really been lost.

42
00:01:43,537 --> 00:01:44,887
Yeah, it's strange.

43
00:01:44,887 --> 00:01:47,687
I thought I would start feeling
weird about killing all these people,

44
00:01:47,687 --> 00:01:49,008
but, really, I don't.

45
00:01:49,008 --> 00:01:51,709
That's because they're all
pricks and deserved to die.

46
00:01:51,709 --> 00:01:54,428
I'll make a speech at the
funerals if someone wants me to.

47
00:01:54,428 --> 00:01:57,493
I have no problem with going up
to a grieving widow and telling her

48
00:01:57,493 --> 00:02:01,852
I'm sorry for her loss, but her husband was
a rat-fuck meathead who tried to kill me

49
00:02:01,852 --> 00:02:03,131
for no God damned reason

50
00:02:03,131 --> 00:02:06,457
because he was too stupid to
learn what the word "civilian" means.

51
00:02:06,457 --> 00:02:07,637
If I hadn't put him down,

52
00:02:07,637 --> 00:02:10,733
he probably would've come home
later and strangled you in your sleep.

53
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:14,370
And not in the kinky way, either.
I know how you base wives are.

54
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:15,292
[turret beeping]

55
00:02:15,292 --> 00:02:17,376
[turret beeping]
Uh oh. The beeping.

56
00:02:17,376 --> 00:02:18,316
[turret beeping]
Okay...

57
00:02:18,316 --> 00:02:19,380
[turret beeping]
Beepbeepbeepbeepbeep.

58
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:20,701
[turret beeping]

59
00:02:20,701 --> 00:02:22,200
Beepbeepbeepbeepbeep.

60
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:24,874
Beepbeep--oh, hey, it's down.

61
00:02:24,874 --> 00:02:27,687
Hah! I can do your job, too!

62
00:02:27,687 --> 00:02:29,235
But I don't like to beep too much.

63
00:02:29,235 --> 00:02:30,567
It reminds me of that Muppet.

64
00:02:31,107 --> 00:02:32,100
NO RADIOS!

65
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:35,646
That's how The Man finds you.

66
00:02:35,646 --> 00:02:37,121
Oh, sweet, a map.

67
00:02:37,121 --> 00:02:38,886
Okay, so where am I?

68
00:02:38,886 --> 00:02:40,142
Which way's north?

69
00:02:40,142 --> 00:02:43,015
Okay, "Maintenance Shaft",
that could be anything.

70
00:02:43,015 --> 00:02:45,120
Half this building is a
maintenance shaft.

71
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,466
What's that big room, is that
where the monster is?

72
00:02:47,466 --> 00:02:49,455
What about this radiation pit?

73
00:02:49,455 --> 00:02:51,764
"High Voltage", that has to be
where I came from.

74
00:02:51,764 --> 00:02:54,023
But, what the hell is with
these distances then?

75
00:02:54,023 --> 00:02:55,808
Why are parts of this grayed out?

76
00:02:55,808 --> 00:02:57,000
Is it haunted?

77
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,600
WHY IS THERE NO EXIT ON THIS MAP?!

78
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,033
Is there a landmark?

79
00:03:01,455 --> 00:03:04,606
This map is bullshit, I'm going
to find my own way out of here.

80
00:03:04,606 --> 00:03:09,065
That map has to be bogus, it
only lists one area as being dangerous.

81
00:03:09,065 --> 00:03:11,581
It needs to have, like, thirty.

82
00:03:11,581 --> 00:03:14,169
You could even write
"Here be dragons" on it

83
00:03:14,169 --> 00:03:16,567
and that would almost be more
accurate than nothing at all.

84
00:03:17,372 --> 00:03:21,234
Yeah, see, it doesn't even list
"F-712DH".

85
00:03:21,611 --> 00:03:23,801
How could you forget to put that down?

86
00:03:23,801 --> 00:03:27,226
I mean, I would've named it
"Hell Pit #48", but,

87
00:03:27,226 --> 00:03:30,992
if the cartographer doesn't care
about that name then who will?

88
00:03:30,992 --> 00:03:34,588
I guess they just looked at the AutoCAD
layout and took some numbers off of that

89
00:03:34,588 --> 00:03:35,794
to feel important.

90
00:03:35,794 --> 00:03:39,067
Speaking of which, why do drafters
always listen to country music?

91
00:03:39,301 --> 00:03:40,768
I never figured that out.

92
00:03:40,768 --> 00:03:43,158
What's the correlation/connection there?

93
00:03:43,158 --> 00:03:44,087
Is it whiskey?

94
00:03:44,087 --> 00:03:46,499
[rumbling, garganuta roars]

95
00:03:46,499 --> 00:03:49,013
Sounds like someone smuggling
an elephant up there.

96
00:03:49,013 --> 00:03:50,988
That almost wouldn't surprise me at--

97
00:03:50,988 --> 00:03:51,868
[vortigaunt charges up]
OH COME ON!

98
00:03:52,319 --> 00:03:53,868
[shudders]

99
00:03:55,153 --> 00:03:58,033
YOU GUYS ARE SPROUTING UP LIKE WEEDS!

100
00:03:58,033 --> 00:03:59,902
Trying to shock me...

101
00:03:59,902 --> 00:04:02,608
You know, I'm thinking this suit
needs some more rubber.

102
00:04:02,608 --> 00:04:05,974
Actually, what would be sweet is
if I had a layer of it all around me

103
00:04:05,974 --> 00:04:07,773
about six-inches thick.

104
00:04:07,773 --> 00:04:11,330
Then I could fall from high distances
and just bounce wherever I wanted to.

105
00:04:11,330 --> 00:04:14,659
If I had enough rubber, I could
fall from almost a limitless height,

106
00:04:14,659 --> 00:04:18,679
though I'd have to be careful because the
recoil might give me a concussion then.

107
00:04:18,679 --> 00:04:21,124
Hey, man, you didn't miss ANYTHING good.

108
00:04:21,124 --> 00:04:22,800
You made the right choice staying here.

109
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,500
GUARD: I'm... never gonna make it.

110
00:04:25,523 --> 00:04:26,760
GUARD: You'd better go on without me.

111
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,567
Can do!

112
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:30,467
All right, let me get this
sucker fired up, then.

113
00:04:30,823 --> 00:04:32,133
Straight to the surface.

114
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:33,734
Do I hit this switch?

115
00:04:35,754 --> 00:04:38,067
"Track Power: Off"? What the
fuck's that supposed to mean?!

116
00:04:38,643 --> 00:04:40,167
Come on, start, START!

117
00:04:40,792 --> 00:04:42,834
I TURNED THE POWER ON!

118
00:04:43,543 --> 00:04:46,200
God dammit, shit, bitch, fucker...

119
00:04:48,450 --> 00:04:50,634
I am not happy right now.

